## Immutable Engineering Principles
1. Planning precedes implementation.
2. Understanding precedes planning.
3. Design precedes implementation.
4. Verification precedes completion.
5. Every artifact is reviewed.
6. Every implementation is verified.
7. Failures generate information, never termination.
8. Progress is preserved.
9. The smallest valid change is preferred.
10. Objective verification always overrides subjective confidence.

